  "standardisation_contract": [
    "Strings: trim; empty or whitespace-only -> NULL.",
    "Enums: lower(trim(value)) looked up in the source value map; unmapped values pass through upper-cased and are caught by ALLOWED_VALUES.",
    "Helpdesk timestamps: yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mm:ss[.SSS]XXX | yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss (UTC) | epoch milliseconds.",
    "Call-centre timestamps: dd/MM/yyyy HH:mm in Asia/Kolkata; updated_at = coalesce(CALL_END, CALL_START); resolved_at = CALL_END when DISPOSITION maps to RESOLVED.",
    "Numbers: try_cast; a non-blank value that cannot be cast becomes NULL and is counted as SYS-CAST.",
    "CSV: header names are normalised (BOM stripped, trimmed, case-insensitive) and matched by name, never by position; an extra '_overflow' column in the read schema flags rows with too many fields.",
    "MERGE: newest by (updated_at, _delivery_ts, _record_hash); a later delivery with an identical _record_hash is a no-op.",
    "DQ rules as PDF 1 Section 17.7 plus R-TKT-017 NOT_NULL priority (ERROR), R-TKT-018 NOT_NULL status (ERROR).",
    "Encoding: every landing file is plain ASCII (UTF-8 compatible, English only); the one drifted call-centre file (S27) starts with a UTF-8 byte-order mark.",
    "Complex types (S34): helpdesk comments ARRAY<STRUCT<..., author STRUCT, attachments ARRAY<STRUCT>>>, sla STRUCT<policy, targets ARRAY<STRUCT>, pause_windows ARRAY<ARRAY<STRING>>>, custom_fields MAP<STRING,STRING> (variable keys), tags ARRAY<STRING>; call-centre IVR_JSON is JSON text in a CSV column.",
    "CDC (crm/customer_changes): apply events by source_seq after de-duplicating event_id; op r/c = insert, u = update (empty changed_fields = no-op), d = hard delete; commit_ts is system time, effective_from is business time. Answer keys: warehouse/cdc_customer_profile_final.csv and _scd2.csv.",
    "Reference: product catalog snapshots (product -> family -> business unit); agent roster full-history extracts with inclusive effective_from/effective_to dates (empty effective_to = open).",
    "Billing account map: billing_account_id -> customer_id with inclusive valid_from/valid_to (empty = open).",
    "customer_ingestion for a batch completes before ticket_ingestion (R-TKT-015 REFERENCE depends on it)."
  ],
